        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: هیجان زده",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هیجان زده (hayajânzade) — \"excited\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچه ها برای سفر هیجان زده هستند. bachchehâ barâ-ye safar hayajânzade hastand. The children are excited about the trip."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hayajân 'excitement' + zade 'struck' (from zadan): struck by excitement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hayajânzade is built in Persian on hayajân, 'excitement', a loan usually traced to Arabic hayajān, 'agitation', and zade, 'struck', from the inherited verb zadan. EtymDB has no entry for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
